Compilation, verifier, and smoke checks pass, but the new utilities fail for the documented default voice configuration and can silently produce incorrect square-format footage when cloning episodes.

Full review comments:

- [P1] Honor the documented default voice — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\scripts\controle_voix.py:46-47
  When an episode omits `voix_off`, `voix.choix()` returns `{}` and this lookup raises `KeyError`; `pub.py` repeats the same assumption at line 78. `render.py` already falls back to `C.VOIX_ID`, and [CLAUDE.md:233] documents this default, so apply the fallback in both utilities.

- [P1] Preserve square B-roll overrides in cloned episodes — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\scripts\pub.py:63-68
  This clone copies only `broll`; when the source has `broll_carre/<fichier>` overrides, the generated `-pub` episode's square render falls back to the normal shot and delivers different footage. `apercu.py` has the same omission, so both clone paths need to preserve square overrides.
